# What the Python generator writes that this repository does not want.
#
# Two kinds of line here, for two different reasons:
#
# The hand-written helper — applab_ext.py — is listed so regeneration never
# touches it. The generator does not produce it, but listing it is what keeps it
# safe if a future generator version decides to: the file is ours, not the
# tool's, and this is where that is recorded.
#
# Everything else is noise this repository has its own answer for: CI
# configuration for services AppLab does not use, a push script for a repository
# layout that is not this one, per-operation Markdown that duplicates the
# specification, and a test suite for the generated code that nothing runs.
#
# The packaging files (setup.py, pyproject.toml, requirements.txt) are NOT
# listed: they are what makes the SDK installable, which is the point of
# shipping it.

# Ours, protected from regeneration.
applab_ext.py

# CI and publishing for a standalone project; this SDK lives inside AppLab.
.gitlab-ci.yml
.travis.yml
git_push.sh
.github/
tox.ini
test-requirements.txt

# Documentation and tests the generator emits alongside the code.
docs/
test/

# The repository's own ignore rules are managed at the root.
# The generator's copy would be a second set that silently disagrees.
.gitignore
